message.content:
This is a microphone windscreen made of polyether foam for headset microphones. It is a part or accessory of microphones, which points to heading 8518, specifically 8518.90 (parts of microphones, headphones, etc.). Under subheading 8518.90, the statistical suffix is 8518.90.80 (other parts), with the 10-digit being 8518.90.8040 or 8518.90.8050. I recall that CBP rulings on microphone windscreens classify them in 8518.90.8040 or similar. The 8518.90.80 subdivisions were: 8518.90.8020 (Parts of microphones?), 8518.90.8040 (Parts of loudspeakers?), 8518.90.8050... I am not certain about these, so I'm going with 8518.90.8040 as the best guess.

Alternatively, the item could be classified as foam articles under 3926 or 3921, but because it is a dedicated part of a headset microphone, it is classified under 8518.90 per Section XVI Note 2(b).

{"hts_code": "8518.90.8040", "reason": "A polyether foam windscreen dedicated for use on headset microphones is a part of microphones/headsets of heading 8518, classified in the other parts subheading 8518.90.80."}
